<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India news: Opposition protest clouds Modi's 25-year milestone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ff9f57c36612dd2afd755519d041c6c1f4386677082951329429b5e1131e677</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-protest-clouds-modi-s-25-year-milestone/live-79570653--dd5c6b9365a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-protest-clouds-modi-s-25-year-milestone/live-79570653?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi police has beefed up security around the Election Commission of India, likely preparing for another day of 'vote theft' protests. Meanwhile, PM Modi marks 25 years in public service. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b6ffe71211f488bdb6a07e8287ca509c00fa5ef4fb3bad2fb8190f7fe4e8cb4</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Mali: Junta forces retake strategic town of Kidal from separatists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eebff7b8ba08c6dec95ea3fa213649be4b33058fffd9aa36893f6be772fadd9</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617--dc7ca7f76853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mali's military regained control of the strategic town of Kidal after forcing Tuareg separatists and al Queda-linked jihadists to withdraw following an offensive backed by Russia's Africa Corps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Lionel Messi plays final game for Argentina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97c64b6915f478ec296d51d7bec20215cee1d5a21eec9ce71d0205613500509c</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-lionel-messi-plays-final-game-for-argentina/a-79570608--6687ff69f964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-lionel-messi-plays-final-game-for-argentina/a-79570608?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentinian superstar Lionel Messi bowed out of international football with one last goal for his country. For football in Argentina, and indeed across the world, it's the end of an era.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Christa Pike awake after failed Tennessee execution: lawyers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09b58d23323fed7807948dbed37124111117f24140d12c98fc3db364c90cf3ea</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T23:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/christa-pike-awake-after-failed-tennessee-execution-lawyers/a-79569867--d6b6e800e10a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/christa-pike-awake-after-failed-tennessee-execution-lawyers/a-79569867?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A death row inmate who survived a botched execution last week is conscious and talking in hospital, according to her lawyers, who want to commute her death sentence to life imprisonment without parole.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d11a3ce61737cd4c73b0db8ef44fb0b550ca0db5313287c7908a8d82ad586a2</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>French AI company announces new, private model</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:831c7f9d14718cefad677a44c838b5170541a732d8f70cdcda85fdcb45547d21</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-ai-company-announces-new-private-model/a-79569597--64cfbccdac1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-ai-company-announces-new-private-model/a-79569597?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The company's new model, named "Le Chonk," is its first release in five months. Mistral says it outruns some of its Chinese competitors in several areas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Naked Trump statue goes on display in Strasbourg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc55634a1f7144664e6607aeb15ee0e73b898c59a8de4ce71357aac37ba0051f</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/naked-trump-statue-goes-on-display-in-strasbourg/a-79568640--b613f03d8e20.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/naked-trump-statue-goes-on-display-in-strasbourg/a-79568640?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Titled "The Orange Plague," a gold-coated statue presents Donald Trump sitting on a smaller man's back. The Danish artist blamed Trump for getting in the way of efforts to address climate change.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:585e85e76e014bd20bad0f9f243b006ee135be456291a4b04e7dada5affd3142</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db0d0b18744aeb54d24e0a4702ae2c0b6976f3abf889f1fab62974a2eab0a61c</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia denies anti-plague measures after pneumonia death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0514f59c286e62b1f40574137269dffe5f369f4eab82d96d0494e8ed8f08f8e5</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-denies-anti-plague-measures-after-pneumonia-death/a-79567922--5a84d749e787.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-denies-anti-plague-measures-after-pneumonia-death/a-79567922?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of an employee at an anti-plague institute in Irkutsk is still being looked into, the authorities said. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio called for Russia to be transparent about its findings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3e1e2660f8324c8de77b6fac58ff55df6f24338e0c96541bf2e65f537950b79</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Seventh arrest made after air base plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa7d6f5f574d714f1e049cc4737ef078a015bd9a5b814232f1b177f79f3f5743</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-seventh-arrest-made-after-air-base-plot/a-79566985--8d48e9554e6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-seventh-arrest-made-after-air-base-plot/a-79566985?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man, a British national in his twenties, was arrested in London in suspicion of "preparing terrorist acts."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e04c722dfebe0e623bd81701c98555239eea94bafb1504476c73a5b7c38154bc</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain court lifts Puigdemont arrest warrant, clearing way for his return home ahead of November elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34eee1a3c29990fb006c464fd2296b7936f3410c509df282f72b0ea134b7358a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-court-lifts-puigdemont-arrest-warrant-clearing-way-for-his-return-home-ahead-of-november-elect/a-79565853--7635b4e28c09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-court-lifts-puigdemont-arrest-warrant-clearing-way-for-his-return-home-ahead-of-november-elections/a-79565853?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Catalan separatist leader Carles Puigdemont fled Spain in 2017 after launching an independence bid. The court's decision means he can return home without fear of arrest after almost a decade in exile.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As more Iranian women reject hijab rules, regime looks at new ways to force compliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c68c9048ffd6eac713dcaf7656f52af929559250eaf071dd2fd2f2433473bb12</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962--9c09f80416a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As more women in Iran reject rules on wearing hijab headscarves, hardliners are shifting focus from "morality police" street enforcement towards social pressure in workplaces, services and businesses.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Southeast Asia's haze crisis: Have lessons been learned?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12d29bc022d2e19276c92ca966f31765c255884ffccdd903900871fdf0da542b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992--f0834d091bdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven years after catastrophic fires prompted promises of tougher action, Southeast Asia is again choking on transboundary haze, raising questions about whether the region has learned the lessons of 2015.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray war may spill over to Eritrea — helped by Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's rhetoric</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7a5e1a0e9468cea713e330075ddceec8a4824387a88ba67bd8666c889ed79bb</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957--f357fb8ada5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed is consolidating power, but he must contend with a regional alliance opposing him and a Tigray conflict that could spill over into Eritrea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD makes history again in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ee49fe54d2f099b4b1d6dc733cd0c431f31e6520a70781072b9f844fbc024de</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146--3b11bbf1dc05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the end of World War II, a German state parliament has chosen parliamentary speaker from the far right: Tobias Rausch of the Alternative for Germany (AfD).</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Literature Prize: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4d72d768c69b4e7a399c2b26556909b9aa3e78b4a68e93809143a2b1a998bea</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--42983d639d88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in Literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Spain approves new emergency housing measures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44d8f1143a6b37193add61de846059d34c43da303cb6589b86dc7a641f8e8720</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-approves-new-emergency-housing-measures/a-79564344--ba63f57648f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-approves-new-emergency-housing-measures/a-79564344?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Spanish government has approved a pair of emergency housing decrees, including extended eviction protections and limits on property speculation, after major protests rocked Barcelona.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
